# Maintainer SSH keys the testnet VPN add-on (setup-vpn.sh) installs for tnadmin.
#
# One line per maintainer key: <name> <fingerprint>
#   <name>         the key file <name>.pub in this directory
#   <fingerprint>  what `ssh-keygen -lf <name>.pub -E sha256` prints (SHA256:...)
# setup-vpn.sh reads only the .pub files listed here, and only when the file holds
# exactly one key with that fingerprint. A .pub file that is not listed is ignored.
#
# Revoking a key: delete its line above the "# revoked:" heading and add a line
#   # revoked: <fingerprint> <name> <date>
# below it. A revoked fingerprint is never installed, even while its .pub file is
# still on disk. Nodes drop the key at the next `setup-vpn.sh --sync-keys` or
# self-heal run after update-scripts.sh. An operator blocks a key on one host with
# a line in /etc/wgvpn/tnadmin.revoked (one fingerprint per line).
